## Overview

This project documents a practical digital forensics laboratory focused on identifying, embedding, extracting, and verifying hidden information using steganography techniques.

---

## Objectives

- Understand steganography and how it differs from encryption.
- Understand basic data-hiding techniques such as LSB (Least Significant Bit).
- Prepare and preserve digital evidence.
- Embed a controlled evidence file into an image.
- Extract hidden data using Steghide.
- Test password recovery using StegSeek.
- Calculate and compare SHA-256 hashes.
- Verify the integrity of recovered evidence.
- Document forensic procedures in a repeatable manner.

